3,Megleno-Romanian language — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/Megleno-Romanian_language,"Megleno-Romanian is classified as an Eastern Romance language within the Indo-European family, specifically belonging to the Balkan Romance subgroup, which also includes Daco-Romanian (the basis of standard Romanian), Aromanian, and Istro-Romanian.","Romanian, Megleno",Indo-European
4,Endangered Languages Project - Megleno-Romanian,https://www.endangeredlanguages.com/lang/3382,"Language metadata. Also known as. Megleno-Rumanian, Meglenitic, Meglenite, Other Roumanian Lects, Romanian, Megleno. CLASSIFICATION. Indo-European, Italic, Romance, Eastern Romance. Code authority. Iso 639-3.","Romanian, Megleno",Indo-European
5,Romanian #84 Most Spoken Language (20M speakers),https://toplangs.com/romanian/,"Aromanian, Megleno-Romanian, and Istro-Romanian. These Balkan Romance varieties are historically related to Romanian. Some scholars group them under the wider Romanian branch, while others treat them as separate languages.","Romanian, Megleno",Indo-European
